<title>SPAIN: Spain to save 700bln ptas with lower interest rate.</title>
<headline>Spain to save 700bln ptas with lower interest rate.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain will save 700 billion pesetas in its 1997 and 1998 budgets thanks to lower long term interest rates on public debt, local media quoted Economy Secretary Cristobal Montoro as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>At a press conference in Salamanca, Montoro said this budget saving together with lower inflation rates would be reflected in a narrowing of the public deficit.</p>
<p>He told reporters: &quot;the credibility of the government's economic policy has been reflected in the financial markets,&quot; adding that long term interest rates had fallen to around seven percent.</p>
<p>Given the trend in these indices, he said he was confident Spain would meet the convergence criteria for European economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
